    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** stands as our strongest play with a score of 56.04. While his base projection is modest, the favorable matchup against Phillips (xERA 4.33) and the boost from hitting in the 5-hole provide the stability we need in a day lacking elite offensive environments. **Taylor Ward** offers high upside with a 52.71 score fueled by a massive 16% park factor boost; however, he carries a 42% rain risk that necessitates close monitoring leading up to first pitch. **Masyn Winn** (50.76) and **Gleyber Torres** (48.51) remain in the lineup to ensure we are maximizing our plate appearance caps, though both are battling negative platoon adjustments that cap their ceilings against their respective right-handed opponents.\n\nThe decision to bench our deeper utility options was straightforward today, largely due to the combination of scheduling gaps and injury status. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Lawrence Butler** are both relegated to the bench due to team off-days, while **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** remain on the IL, limiting our active depth. **Tyler Freeman**, **Bryson Stott**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** were all considered, but none presented a matchup profile that could surpass the daily efficiency scores of our current starting four. We are playing for marginal gains today while protecting our total games played allocation for the remainder of the week.",
